WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:05.422
16 YEARS AGO

2
00:00:05.506 --> 00:00:07.799
<i>Our VIP and his family</i>
<i>are in the suite.</i>

3
00:00:07.883 --> 00:00:11.094
<i>There are also three rebels.</i>
<i>Extract the VIP and family.</i>

4
00:00:11.178 --> 00:00:12.971
<i>If you can't. we're going in.</i>

5
00:00:13.055 --> 00:00:14.097
Copy that.

6
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:22.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

7
00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:28.528
Hands up.

8
00:01:08.694 --> 00:01:09.695
Get out.

9
00:01:13.031 --> 00:01:15.450
<i>There are far more hostages</i>
<i>than we anticipated.</i>

10
00:01:15.534 --> 00:01:17.828
including Koreans and other nationalities.

11
00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:19.788
The operation is too much of a risk.

12
00:01:20.581 --> 00:01:24.251
<i>Concentrate on extracting the VIP.</i>
<i>He's our top priority.</i>

13
00:01:24.334 --> 00:01:25.335
It's not safe.

14
00:01:26.461 --> 00:01:28.797
Some of the hostages
are disguised as terrorists.

15
00:01:29.548 --> 00:01:30.674
<i>Are you certain?</i>

16
00:01:34.595 --> 00:01:38.724
We can't delay this operation any longer
based on unconfirmed information.

17
00:01:39.641 --> 00:01:42.519
Taking down five terrorists
isn't a problem for us.

18
00:01:45.439 --> 00:01:46.606
Don't you agree?

19
00:01:49.234 --> 00:01:50.360
Let's go.

20
00:01:56.074 --> 00:01:57.284
<i>Move in.</i>

21
00:01:57.367 --> 00:01:59.202
<i>You can't. It's too dangerous.</i>

22
00:01:59.286 --> 00:02:01.788
<i>We need to act</i>
<i>before there are more casualties.</i>

23
00:02:01.872 --> 00:02:02.998
<i>Move in.</i>

24
00:02:03.081 --> 00:02:05.667
<i>J. don't go! Don't do it!</i>

25
00:02:07.919 --> 00:02:09.796
- We're moving in.
<i>- I said no!</i>

26
00:03:34.172 --> 00:03:36.383
Stay here. I'll come back.

27
00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:42.222
<i>I remember.</i>

28
00:03:43.265 --> 00:03:44.266
<i>Jeong Jinman.</i>

29
00:03:59.448 --> 00:04:00.824
SIGMA CONFIDENTIAL PROFILE

30
00:04:11.418 --> 00:04:13.420
My hotel is just around the corner.

31
00:04:14.004 --> 00:04:16.089
My schedule is a bit tight.

32
00:04:16.173 --> 00:04:19.843
-Wanna stop?
-No. please. do continue.

33
00:04:19.926 --> 00:04:21.428
Tight is good!

34
00:04:24.556 --> 00:04:26.308
There's a Russian saying.

35
00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:29.519
Live like you're friends with the bear.

36
00:04:29.603 --> 00:04:31.188
But hold onto an ax.

37
00:04:31.271 --> 00:04:35.650
I have never met a Japanese woman
who knows a Russian proverb.

38
00:04:35.734 --> 00:04:37.194
I like bears.

39
00:04:37.903 --> 00:04:39.696
They are wild.

40
00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:41.281
But cute.

41
00:04:41.364 --> 00:04:42.699
Like you. Dimitri.

42
00:04:49.539 --> 00:04:52.000
You shouldn't steal from Babylon…

43
00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:54.628
Dimitri.

44
00:04:54.711 --> 00:04:56.713
You fucking bitch!

45
00:05:13.897 --> 00:05:16.733
Is the drug working?

46
00:05:18.318 --> 00:05:20.570
- The DJ isn't great tonight.
- Agreed.

47
00:05:20.654 --> 00:05:22.531
Give me your lipstick.

48
00:05:25.033 --> 00:05:26.993
What's that noise? A guy?

49
00:05:34.835 --> 00:05:36.294
Get a hotel room!

50
00:05:37.045 --> 00:05:39.256
Why? I like doing it here too.

51
00:05:39.339 --> 00:05:40.590
What?

52
00:05:40.674 --> 00:05:42.008
Seriously?

53
00:05:42.092 --> 00:05:44.427
No. for real.
What are they doing in there?

54
00:05:44.511 --> 00:05:46.054
This is the women's restroom.

55
00:06:00.402 --> 00:06:02.362
All good. I took him out.

56
00:06:02.445 --> 00:06:04.781
Get someone over here to clean this up.

57
00:06:04.865 --> 00:06:07.784
<i>The director said to get back</i>
<i>to the team ASAP.</i>

58
00:06:07.868 --> 00:06:09.452
Mm-hmm. Yeah. okay.

59
00:06:14.165 --> 00:06:17.043
CONFIDENTIAL PROFILE PERSONAL
PROFILE NAME JEONG JINMAN

60
00:06:17.127 --> 00:06:19.504
CONFIDENTIAL PROFILE PERSONAL
PROFILE NAME JEONG JIAN

61
00:06:21.965 --> 00:06:24.718
JEONG JI-AN

62
00:06:26.344 --> 00:06:27.345
Jian?

63
00:07:34.704 --> 00:07:36.665
The operation's a failure!

64
00:07:57.769 --> 00:08:00.689
Rescuing the hostage is the top priority.

65
00:08:01.648 --> 00:08:04.567
Why did you jump out in front
when you're the team leader?

66
00:08:05.318 --> 00:08:07.696
While you were busy playing the hero.

67
00:08:08.571 --> 00:08:10.365
your team was wiped out.

68
00:08:11.908 --> 00:08:15.662
Hey. by the way.
why'd you make this guy the hostage?

69
00:08:15.745 --> 00:08:17.872
Wasn't it supposed to be a little kid?

70
00:08:20.667 --> 00:08:21.835
L.

71
00:08:22.377 --> 00:08:24.045
How come you didn't rescue M?

72
00:08:24.129 --> 00:08:26.172
Sorry. Q killed me.

73
00:08:26.923 --> 00:08:28.216
<i>Oneechan.</i>

74
00:08:28.842 --> 00:08:30.135
Not fair.

75
00:08:30.218 --> 00:08:32.887
Why'd you come? You weren't supposed
to be part of this operation.

76
00:08:32.971 --> 00:08:36.808
Hm… As the leader.
you should always be prepared. right?

77
00:08:36.891 --> 00:08:37.976
Wow. Good one.

78
00:08:41.271 --> 00:08:42.731
We have a new mission.

79
00:08:43.481 --> 00:08:44.482
J.

80
00:08:44.566 --> 00:08:46.526
L. M.

81
00:08:46.609 --> 00:08:48.528
X. Marco.

82
00:08:48.611 --> 00:08:51.614
Be at Kansai Airport
by 9:00 a.m. tomorrow.

83
00:08:52.282 --> 00:08:54.826
The operations brief
will begin once we arrive.

84
00:08:55.994 --> 00:08:59.414
Let me know if you need personal firearms.
I'll send them through my company.

85
00:08:59.497 --> 00:09:00.874
Where's the operation area?

86
00:09:03.501 --> 00:09:04.502
Korea.

87
00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:09.049
A SHOP FOR KILLERS 2

88
00:09:16.931 --> 00:09:19.851
EPISODE 03
PAST IS PAST. PRESENT IS PRESENT

89
00:09:34.949 --> 00:09:36.785
MURTHEHELP

90
00:09:38.912 --> 00:09:41.998
We've been getting
a lot of reports lately about smuggling.

91
00:09:43.083 --> 00:09:44.292
Smuggling what?

92
00:09:44.375 --> 00:09:46.461
Why would anybody
wanna smuggle something here?

93
00:09:48.254 --> 00:09:50.340
I'm done with the search. Nothing here.

94
00:09:50.423 --> 00:09:51.549
All right.
let's head home.

95
00:09:51.633 --> 00:09:52.717
Yes. sir.

96
00:09:53.051 --> 00:09:57.305
Oh. Is that the girlfriend
the ladies were talking about?

97
00:09:57.680 --> 00:10:00.475
Oh! A midnight date?

98
00:10:00.558 --> 00:10:02.352
What girlfriend? Have a good night.

99
00:10:02.435 --> 00:10:04.062
-Nice to meet you. miss!
-Time to go home. please.

100
00:10:04.145 --> 00:10:06.397
Woojin is finally
getting married. huh?

101
00:10:06.481 --> 00:10:07.732
Goodbye.

102
00:10:12.570 --> 00:10:13.905
Miss Arin.

103
00:10:13.988 --> 00:10:14.989
Arin.

104
00:10:29.921 --> 00:10:31.214
MURTHEHELP

105
00:10:37.762 --> 00:10:39.639
{\an8}MURTHEHELP SEARCH

106
00:11:02.078 --> 00:11:05.373
BROTHER JEONG JINMAN MASTER PASIN

107
00:11:19.053 --> 00:11:20.471
Uh. Miss Arin.

108
00:11:21.431 --> 00:11:24.058
-Can I explain what happened?
-That won't be necessary.

109
00:11:24.142 --> 00:11:25.518
I'm not interested.

110
00:11:32.525 --> 00:11:34.444
-Still. I--
-I said I don't care.

111
00:11:35.403 --> 00:11:37.071
I'm not even curious about it.

112
00:11:40.617 --> 00:11:42.118
Right.

113
00:11:42.202 --> 00:11:43.328
Sorry about that.

114
00:12:17.654 --> 00:12:23.159
Jian. do you think running away
is gonna change anything? Hm?

115
00:12:23.493 --> 00:12:25.245
What am I supposed to do?

116
00:12:36.297 --> 00:12:41.469
<i>Jeong Jian. from now on.</i>
<i>you have to stay alive on your own.</i>

117
00:12:50.853 --> 00:12:53.690
<i>This bag here.</i>
<i>just… once you get somewhere safe.</i>

118
00:12:53.773 --> 00:12:55.233
<i>Open it when you're alone.</i>

119
00:12:59.112 --> 00:13:02.365
READ CAREFULLY JEONG JIAN

120
00:14:36.292 --> 00:14:39.796
<i>What did Jeong Jinman do for them</i>
<i>to call us all the way here?</i>

121
00:14:39.879 --> 00:14:43.216
You took someone out in Korea didn't you?

122
00:14:43.299 --> 00:14:44.550
Yeah.

123
00:14:44.634 --> 00:14:47.470
During the exhausting
day-trip boat mission.

124
00:14:47.553 --> 00:14:50.723
That guy was Jeong Jinman's old boss.

125
00:14:52.517 --> 00:14:57.271
It seems like Jeong Jinman
has decided to become a traitor.

126
00:14:59.065 --> 00:15:00.066
Interesting.

127
00:15:00.775 --> 00:15:02.860
They forced him out of the company.

128
00:15:06.614 --> 00:15:08.241
This is karma.

129
00:15:08.324 --> 00:15:09.450
What?

130
00:15:10.952 --> 00:15:13.579
-What do you mean?
-Think about it.

131
00:15:13.663 --> 00:15:16.666
You told Babylon about Jeong Jinman.
Said to recruit him.

132
00:15:16.749 --> 00:15:20.378
But now. here we are
coming to Korea to capture him.

133
00:15:20.461 --> 00:15:21.963
Definitely karma.

134
00:15:22.046 --> 00:15:26.342
Hey. If Jeong Jinman wasn't there.
you definitely would've died.

135
00:15:27.135 --> 00:15:30.638
The past is the past.
and the present is the present.

136
00:15:33.516 --> 00:15:35.810
Oh. Is that the place?

137
00:15:45.736 --> 00:15:47.905
Stay here. I'll come back.

138
00:15:49.198 --> 00:15:51.993
STAFF ONLY

139
00:16:08.676 --> 00:16:10.678
Stay there!

140
00:16:11.554 --> 00:16:12.763
Just sit down. sit down!

141
00:16:12.847 --> 00:16:15.808
- How many are there?
<i>- Two dead. three remaining.</i>

142
00:16:15.892 --> 00:16:17.852
<i>Two in front of the door.</i>
<i>one inside the room.</i>

143
00:16:19.395 --> 00:16:20.396
Jun.

144
00:16:22.190 --> 00:16:23.357
Jun!

145
00:16:27.320 --> 00:16:28.404
Bang!

146
00:16:33.701 --> 00:16:35.536
Shut up. shut up!

147
00:16:56.933 --> 00:16:59.185
We're from Korea. Don't be scared.

148
00:17:02.939 --> 00:17:04.982
Put the gun down. Or she will die.

149
00:17:05.900 --> 00:17:07.318
-Drop the gun.
-Help me!

150
00:17:07.401 --> 00:17:08.986
I said drop it!

151
00:17:10.738 --> 00:17:14.075
I have a child. Please!

152
00:17:14.158 --> 00:17:15.368
Please let me go!

153
00:17:16.244 --> 00:17:17.245
Please!

154
00:17:18.496 --> 00:17:19.914
Please!

155
00:17:23.209 --> 00:17:24.752
No. Please.

156
00:17:37.390 --> 00:17:38.975
-Make way. make way.
-Thanks for saving us.

157
00:17:39.058 --> 00:17:40.226
Yes. sir.
I'm taking the hostages now.

158
00:17:40.309 --> 00:17:42.061
-Our pleasure.
-Mm-hmm. Thank you.

159
00:17:42.144 --> 00:17:44.313
You'll be assisted back home
by the embassy.

160
00:17:44.397 --> 00:17:46.774
That's what you get
for not listening to me.

161
00:17:46.857 --> 00:17:48.442
What else was I supposed to do?

162
00:17:48.526 --> 00:17:51.195
You gotta stand down
when I tell you not to move in!

163
00:17:54.282 --> 00:17:57.660
You'll get yourself into hot water
if you keep being so reckless.

164
00:17:58.828 --> 00:18:00.746
-J. are you okay?
-Yeah. I'm fine.

165
00:18:00.830 --> 00:18:04.041
Kusanagi Jin. Team leader of Babylon.

166
00:18:04.875 --> 00:18:06.627
Nobody goes harder than you.

167
00:18:06.711 --> 00:18:10.298
Jinman Jeong. Master Sergeant
of Korean Special Forces.

168
00:18:10.381 --> 00:18:12.508
Business as usual. right?

169
00:18:12.592 --> 00:18:15.886
It would've been nice
if Korean Forces had informed us.

170
00:18:15.970 --> 00:18:19.265
It caused us confusion in our operation.
and we almost lost the mission.

171
00:18:19.348 --> 00:18:20.808
Are you Korean?

172
00:18:20.891 --> 00:18:22.435
Something like that.

173
00:18:24.312 --> 00:18:27.398
- Yeah. it's cute.
- Wanna wear it?

174
00:18:27.481 --> 00:18:28.691
-No. thanks.
-Try it on.

175
00:18:28.774 --> 00:18:30.735
Hey. J. maybe you should've worn
it instead of Q.

176
00:18:30.818 --> 00:18:33.946
Hard to say. Without confirming
with our Special Forces beforehand.

177
00:18:34.030 --> 00:18:36.490
rushing in could've harmed
the foreign hostages.

178
00:18:36.574 --> 00:18:37.575
What?

179
00:18:37.908 --> 00:18:39.702
Please take over for me.

180
00:18:41.203 --> 00:18:43.497
What? Uh. Jinman where are you going?

181
00:18:46.334 --> 00:18:47.335
Let's go!

182
00:18:49.712 --> 00:18:53.090
I didn't get to introduce
myself. Q is what they call me.

183
00:18:54.008 --> 00:18:55.134
I'm Jeong Jinman.

184
00:18:56.093 --> 00:18:57.303
Your Korean is good.

185
00:18:57.470 --> 00:19:01.057
Ah. I have a Korean friend in Osaka.

186
00:19:01.140 --> 00:19:03.434
- I've been studying.
- Oh. I see.

187
00:19:04.644 --> 00:19:08.522
The operation was classified.
so I couldn't say anything.

188
00:19:08.606 --> 00:19:10.399
- I'm sorry.
- I understand.

189
00:19:13.110 --> 00:19:15.988
Is that him?
The person who saved me?

190
00:19:20.826 --> 00:19:21.827
Thank you.

191
00:19:23.829 --> 00:19:24.830
Thank you.

192
00:19:29.126 --> 00:19:30.961
I'll come back
to work right away.

193
00:19:31.045 --> 00:19:32.922
Don't come to the hospital. It's a hassle.

194
00:19:33.005 --> 00:19:35.883
- I'll be there later. so behave yourself.
- What?

195
00:19:37.259 --> 00:19:40.304
That hurts.

196
00:19:41.972 --> 00:19:44.850
Uh… I. um…

197
00:19:46.519 --> 00:19:49.021
I really appreciate what you did.

198
00:19:49.647 --> 00:19:52.858
Would… you like to get a drink?

199
00:19:55.528 --> 00:19:56.570
The drink is on me.

200
00:19:56.654 --> 00:19:58.364
We'll be leaving the country
in a few hours.

201
00:19:58.447 --> 00:20:00.199
It was an unofficial operation.

202
00:20:02.243 --> 00:20:03.369
Ah…

203
00:20:04.537 --> 00:20:05.621
Okay.

204
00:20:06.997 --> 00:20:11.627
-Then. um. then have a safe flight.
-You did a good job.

205
00:20:15.089 --> 00:20:16.757
You're just gonna leave like that?

206
00:20:22.513 --> 00:20:23.514
Excuse me.

207
00:20:25.266 --> 00:20:26.267
Yes?

208
00:20:35.234 --> 00:20:37.653
The next time we meet.
we'll go have a drink together.

209
00:20:38.612 --> 00:20:40.322
Either in Japan or Korea.

210
00:20:48.414 --> 00:20:50.332
Hello.

211
00:20:50.416 --> 00:20:52.918
I look forward to your kind operation.
Thank you.

212
00:20:53.002 --> 00:20:56.255
Hey. They'll think we're pushovers
if you do that.

213
00:20:56.338 --> 00:20:59.300
I'm just honey trapping
to help lower their guard a little.

214
00:20:59.383 --> 00:21:01.761
How are you honey trapping
without any honey?

215
00:21:04.054 --> 00:21:06.640
Hey. Don't forget.
just because we're here.

216
00:21:06.724 --> 00:21:09.435
doesn't mean that we should be bulldogs.

217
00:21:09.518 --> 00:21:14.148
Leadership isn't coerced.
It's something you have to earn.

218
00:21:16.317 --> 00:21:17.651
Nice to meet you.

219
00:21:22.281 --> 00:21:23.407
Oh. shit…

220
00:21:29.538 --> 00:21:30.748
Gross.

221
00:21:30.831 --> 00:21:32.249
Why does it smell musty?

222
00:21:33.834 --> 00:21:35.503
I know it's not ideal.

223
00:21:36.337 --> 00:21:37.880
This is our accommodation.

224
00:21:38.923 --> 00:21:40.216
Make the best of it.

225
00:21:43.385 --> 00:21:44.595
Somebody's in there.

226
00:22:10.120 --> 00:22:11.497
You're the ones?

227
00:22:15.918 --> 00:22:18.754
You came all the way across the sea
to capture Jeong Jinman?

228
00:22:24.468 --> 00:22:25.469
Hello.

229
00:22:26.095 --> 00:22:28.013
I'm Q. The team lead.

230
00:22:28.764 --> 00:22:29.890
A woman?

231
00:22:40.651 --> 00:22:41.694
Hey. one-eye.

232
00:22:42.319 --> 00:22:44.572
I don't have to know what you're saying

233
00:22:44.655 --> 00:22:47.241
to understand that your tone
is damn cocky.

234
00:23:09.179 --> 00:23:10.723
It's unbelievable.

235
00:23:10.806 --> 00:23:12.933
They made off with the entire server…

236
00:23:13.183 --> 00:23:16.687
…and nothing's happened yet?

237
00:23:16.770 --> 00:23:18.188
That's really weird.

238
00:23:18.272 --> 00:23:21.275
All the confidential data
on the server is encrypted.

239
00:23:21.942 --> 00:23:24.528
Just because Jeong Jinman has the server.

240
00:23:24.612 --> 00:23:26.989
doesn't mean
he'll be able to un-encrypt it.

241
00:23:27.072 --> 00:23:30.034
Either Jinman hasn't cracked the code…

242
00:23:31.452 --> 00:23:33.913
or he's honoring the agreement
to ceasefire.

243
00:23:33.996 --> 00:23:37.041
Jeong Jinman made that promise
on his own.

244
00:23:37.124 --> 00:23:40.794
The company won't consider
tolerating even a one percent risk.

245
00:23:40.878 --> 00:23:43.088
What's the status of progress?

246
00:23:43.923 --> 00:23:45.299
This.

247
00:23:45.382 --> 00:23:47.801
Jeong Jinman's website
is currently under construction.

248
00:23:47.885 --> 00:23:53.557
We are using his own system against him.
and developed a murthehelp app in secret.

249
00:23:53.641 --> 00:23:56.143
Think of it as a secondhand marketplace
for weapons.

250
00:23:56.226 --> 00:23:59.188
Jeong Jinman controlled everything
on the website.

251
00:23:59.271 --> 00:24:01.857
but the app operates
as more of an open marketplace.

252
00:24:01.941 --> 00:24:04.485
As the number of users grow.
the data grows with it.

253
00:24:04.568 --> 00:24:09.406
On the surface level. this app appears
to have no relationship with Babylon.

254
00:24:09.490 --> 00:24:11.909
- Jeong Jinman's niece?
- Correct.

255
00:24:11.992 --> 00:24:12.993
Jeong Jian.

