502
00:44:13.609 --> 00:44:14.902
and looking after Woojin.

503
00:44:15.653 --> 00:44:18.531
That's why he never left the island
even though he should.

504
00:44:18.614 --> 00:44:22.034
He's always right beside us.
taking care of us like we did for him.

505
00:44:22.743 --> 00:44:26.998
And so that's how Woojin
became our island's "son."

506
00:44:29.667 --> 00:44:32.879
-Hey. you're the same age. right?
-Huh?

507
00:44:32.962 --> 00:44:35.882
Why are you two so formal with each other?

508
00:44:35.965 --> 00:44:39.427
"If you wouldn't mind.
And thank you so much." Like that?

509
00:44:40.511 --> 00:44:45.141
"Miss Arin. Mr. Woojin."
You can't be serious.

510
00:44:45.224 --> 00:44:46.976
It's cringy.

511
00:44:47.059 --> 00:44:49.395
Just talk casually.

512
00:44:59.030 --> 00:45:01.199
Um. please check it.

513
00:45:07.914 --> 00:45:08.915
Here.

514
00:45:14.045 --> 00:45:16.130
That's the ID and password
for the app.

515
00:45:16.214 --> 00:45:17.215
I got it from the captain.

516
00:45:17.298 --> 00:45:20.218
but I'm not sure
how the verification process works.

517
00:45:20.968 --> 00:45:23.304
I tried it yesterday.
but it blocked me out.

518
00:45:31.395 --> 00:45:32.772
Have you eaten yet?

519
00:45:37.401 --> 00:45:38.736
What?

520
00:45:39.737 --> 00:45:42.823
The <i>samgyeopsal…</i>

521
00:45:47.078 --> 00:45:48.913
There's too much to eat by myself.

522
00:45:50.331 --> 00:45:51.916
Wanna eat together?

523
00:45:53.084 --> 00:45:54.418
Uh…

524
00:46:04.345 --> 00:46:06.222
Oh. you go first.

525
00:46:16.232 --> 00:46:17.566
Try it.

526
00:46:17.650 --> 00:46:20.569
Auntie Jeomrye's <i>meongge-jeot</i>
is really good with it.

527
00:46:38.212 --> 00:46:40.047
Are you going to turn yourself in?

528
00:46:47.763 --> 00:46:49.348
Yeah. I am.

529
00:46:49.432 --> 00:46:52.310
Who's going to take care of
the aunties' supplies when you're gone?

530
00:46:57.857 --> 00:46:59.108
I'll keep it a secret.

531
00:47:00.151 --> 00:47:01.193
Don't turn yourself in.

532
00:47:08.492 --> 00:47:11.912
I appreciate that.
Thank you so much. Miss Arin.

533
00:47:14.874 --> 00:47:16.292
That's a load off.

534
00:47:16.375 --> 00:47:18.711
I've been so worried about the aunties.
I haven't been sleeping.

535
00:47:18.794 --> 00:47:21.797
Just make sure that you don't get caught
from now on.

536
00:47:23.299 --> 00:47:24.300
Uh-huh.

537
00:47:25.051 --> 00:47:26.052
Okay.

538
00:47:39.857 --> 00:47:42.985
Well. since. um…

539
00:47:43.819 --> 00:47:46.447
you seem to know all of my secrets now.

540
00:47:47.823 --> 00:47:49.658
how about you tell me one of yours?

541
00:47:50.326 --> 00:47:52.578
-I'm curious about yours.
-What?

542
00:47:56.123 --> 00:47:57.124
That.

543
00:48:02.588 --> 00:48:04.673
You don't have to tell me
if it's uncomfortable.

544
00:48:06.258 --> 00:48:09.178
I probably crossed the line. I apologize.

545
00:48:09.261 --> 00:48:11.722
Someone might try to come and kill me.

546
00:48:12.139 --> 00:48:13.432
I'm preparing for that.

547
00:48:14.100 --> 00:48:17.019
My uncle taught me to defend myself
since I was little.

548
00:48:17.895 --> 00:48:19.688
That's why I run every day.

549
00:48:19.772 --> 00:48:21.816
If someone comes after me. I can escape.

550
00:48:26.070 --> 00:48:27.947
My parents died when I was pretty young.

551
00:48:28.030 --> 00:48:30.408
and so my uncle was forced
to raise me instead.

552
00:48:31.867 --> 00:48:35.079
Hm. He did his best to raise me
in his own way.

553
00:48:36.997 --> 00:48:39.041
But I got scared so I ran away.

554
00:48:40.835 --> 00:48:41.836
Why?

555
00:48:42.670 --> 00:48:44.547
Is your uncle a scary person?

556
00:48:50.553 --> 00:48:52.012
That's not what I meant.

557
00:48:56.434 --> 00:48:59.728
My uncle's a good person.
he's just bad at expressing himself.

558
00:49:00.855 --> 00:49:03.315
That's all. I'll leave it at that.

559
00:49:04.275 --> 00:49:07.194
Sure. yeah.
I appreciate you sharing with me.

560
00:49:09.405 --> 00:49:10.865
Should we talk more casually?

561
00:49:12.491 --> 00:49:13.492
What?

562
00:49:14.452 --> 00:49:16.078
The aunties said we're the same age.

563
00:49:16.162 --> 00:49:17.329
I'm 22.

564
00:49:17.413 --> 00:49:19.373
I'm 22. Miss Arin.

565
00:49:21.167 --> 00:49:24.962
-Whoa…
-There's crumbs on your mouth. sir.

566
00:49:34.054 --> 00:49:35.222
Go on. eat more.

567
00:49:47.651 --> 00:49:49.904
Yong. I hear
there are more than 30 islands

568
00:49:49.987 --> 00:49:51.238
around here alone.

569
00:49:51.322 --> 00:49:54.325
I don't think this is the way to find her.

570
00:49:54.408 --> 00:49:59.330
First. we find the punk
who took our stuff and disappeared.

571
00:50:00.581 --> 00:50:01.624
Then next…

572
00:50:03.209 --> 00:50:04.210
we find this girl.

573
00:50:04.293 --> 00:50:07.671
{\an8}$2.000.000 DOLLAR/CASH
 FEBRUARY 11. 2003

574
00:50:21.185 --> 00:50:22.478
- Arin!
- Oh. my God!

575
00:50:23.354 --> 00:50:24.897
What are you doing?

576
00:50:24.980 --> 00:50:26.899
You said that you're scared.

577
00:50:26.982 --> 00:50:30.277
I thought you'd be less scared
if we ran together.

578
00:50:33.155 --> 00:50:34.907
I didn't say I was scared.

579
00:51:02.893 --> 00:51:04.603
SEASONED SQUID JEOTGAL
I MADE IT. YOU ENJOY IT.

580
00:51:04.687 --> 00:51:07.106
Even if there's soda
in the South Sea.

581
00:51:07.189 --> 00:51:10.317
you can't drink it if
you don't have a cup.

582
00:51:10.401 --> 00:51:13.195
Did I poke your side first.
saying we should live together?

583
00:51:13.279 --> 00:51:16.031
You kept poking first.
saying we should live together!

584
00:51:17.491 --> 00:51:21.078
Oh my. Arin knows how to laugh. after all?

585
00:51:21.161 --> 00:51:24.915
Arin. you are so pretty when you smile.

586
00:51:25.708 --> 00:51:29.587
Cute girl. Smile! Smile and live well.

587
00:51:36.218 --> 00:51:38.262
<i>You don't have to run</i>
<i>with me to my house.</i>

588
00:51:38.345 --> 00:51:40.264
<i>You have to go all the way back home.</i>

589
00:51:40.347 --> 00:51:43.601
It's all right. I enjoy doing it.

590
00:51:43.684 --> 00:51:44.935
See you in the morning.

591
00:52:09.543 --> 00:52:10.878
-Take this.
-Keep it like that.

592
00:52:10.961 --> 00:52:12.171
-Reel it in.
-Hold tight.

593
00:52:13.631 --> 00:52:15.257
You need to buy gochujang.

594
00:52:15.341 --> 00:52:16.592
What else can I get you?

595
00:52:17.426 --> 00:52:19.678
-How much is this?
-Hi. Ma'am. It's 3.000.

596
00:52:19.762 --> 00:52:20.763
- Oh. Arin.
- What?

597
00:52:20.846 --> 00:52:22.723
- Hey. Woojin! Give Arin a ride.
- No. I'm working.

598
00:52:22.806 --> 00:52:24.767
Get on. you're done.
get outta here. get outta here.

599
00:52:24.850 --> 00:52:26.769
Hold his waist real tight.

600
00:52:26.852 --> 00:52:28.354
Go. have a good time.

601
00:52:29.313 --> 00:52:30.981
Just be careful!

602
00:52:36.987 --> 00:52:39.865
IT'S EXACTLY TO MY TASTE.
I ENJOYED IT VERY MUCH - GRANDMA JEOMRYE

603
00:52:58.884 --> 00:53:01.261
HANAM-DO ISLAND
COMMUNITY UNITY FESTIVAL

604
00:53:24.618 --> 00:53:28.664
Did you think we wouldn't find out
that you sold our stuff somewhere else?

605
00:53:29.581 --> 00:53:30.791
You disappeared.

606
00:53:52.187 --> 00:53:53.814
No need to be afraid.

607
00:53:57.401 --> 00:53:58.527
This girl.

608
00:54:00.487 --> 00:54:02.698
I might forget about how you screwed me…

609
00:54:03.657 --> 00:54:05.617
{\an8}If you tell me where to find her.

610
00:54:08.287 --> 00:54:09.496
I envy you.

611
00:54:11.874 --> 00:54:12.916
Why?

612
00:54:13.584 --> 00:54:15.544
Even though you're not related.

613
00:54:15.627 --> 00:54:18.714
you grew up with all the aunties
and uncles all caring about you.

614
00:54:19.548 --> 00:54:20.674
You're so loved.

615
00:54:26.722 --> 00:54:28.682
I grew up living with my uncle.

616
00:54:31.643 --> 00:54:32.853
But I never…

617
00:54:34.646 --> 00:54:36.148
It never felt like…

618
00:54:39.693 --> 00:54:41.153
I was loved.

619
00:54:44.031 --> 00:54:46.366
Like I was always a burden to my uncle.

620
00:54:49.036 --> 00:54:50.454
It just felt like that.

621
00:54:52.956 --> 00:54:56.210
From my uncle's perspective.
he could disappear any time.

622
00:54:56.293 --> 00:54:59.046
so he wanted me to be able
to survive on my own.

623
00:55:00.339 --> 00:55:02.341
That's why he raised me to be tough.

624
00:55:07.095 --> 00:55:09.014
Sometimes I understand.

625
00:55:12.226 --> 00:55:14.603
But other times. I don't really want to.

626
00:55:20.025 --> 00:55:21.693
The present is what counts now. right?

627
00:55:22.569 --> 00:55:23.779
Hm?

628
00:55:25.447 --> 00:55:26.657
The past is the past.

629
00:55:26.740 --> 00:55:30.619
You came here
and you've been loved ever since then.

630
00:55:32.079 --> 00:55:33.247
A whole lot.

631
00:55:38.210 --> 00:55:39.211
I mean. yeah.

632
00:55:40.712 --> 00:55:42.172
I didn't realize at first.

633
00:55:42.256 --> 00:55:44.758
but all the aunties
have been so affectionate.

634
00:55:48.762 --> 00:55:49.763
I didn't…

635
00:55:52.474 --> 00:55:53.559
mean them.

636
00:55:57.646 --> 00:55:59.398
I meant that you're being loved…

637
00:56:01.233 --> 00:56:02.234
by me.

638
00:56:57.331 --> 00:56:58.624
Jeong Jian.

639
00:57:06.590 --> 00:57:07.591
Who are you?

640
00:57:12.679 --> 00:57:16.141
You ran away with our guns. didn't you?

641
00:57:18.435 --> 00:57:20.103
There's the guy.

642
00:57:20.187 --> 00:57:22.397
We tracked her down
and now we get him as well.

643
00:57:22.481 --> 00:57:24.858
It's killing two birds with one stone.

644
00:57:24.941 --> 00:57:26.568
Let's take care of them quickly.

645
00:57:27.736 --> 00:57:28.737
Woojin.

646
00:57:29.488 --> 00:57:30.697
When I count to three.

647
00:57:30.781 --> 00:57:32.908
keep your head down.
and run straight ahead.

648
00:57:33.909 --> 00:57:36.578
-What? Straight ahead?
-Three!

649
00:57:45.212 --> 00:57:46.588
Woojin. get up. quick!

650
00:57:47.964 --> 00:57:49.049
We can't kill her.

651
00:58:00.519 --> 00:58:01.520
Arin!

652
00:58:10.028 --> 00:58:11.530
FRONT TOWARD ENEMY

653
00:58:55.866 --> 00:58:57.451
Arin…

654
00:58:57.534 --> 00:58:59.161
what is all this?

655
00:59:02.539 --> 00:59:04.166
I'll explain everything later.

656
00:59:52.297 --> 00:59:53.715
Shit.

657
01:00:15.403 --> 01:00:17.113
Fucking bitch!

658
01:00:17.197 --> 01:00:18.406
When I catch you.

659
01:00:18.490 --> 01:00:20.867
I'll rip you to shreds.

660
01:00:25.747 --> 01:00:28.708
Yong! Help me out here!

661
01:00:32.128 --> 01:00:34.506
You're no ordinary bitch. are you?

662
01:00:34.589 --> 01:00:36.007
It's all right. Woojin.

663
01:00:41.888 --> 01:00:43.473
You little rats.

664
01:01:19.342 --> 01:01:24.097
A SHOP FOR KILLERS 2

665
01:01:32.188 --> 01:01:33.607
BASED ON THE NOVEL BY KANG JI YOUNG

666
01:01:34.305 --> 01:02:34.425
